# ET Open Rules — Suricata 6.0.4
#
# These rules are managed by suricata-update and downloaded automatically
# from https://rules.emergingthreats.net/open/suricata-6.0/emerging.rules.tar.gz
#
# At the time of the TD3 capture (2026-03-06), 48,795 signatures were loaded.
# The ruleset includes the following categories (sample):
#   - ET SCAN   — port scans, Nmap, reconnaissance
#   - ET WEB    — web exploit patterns, SQLi, XSS
#   - ET MALWARE — known C2 traffic, bot signatures
#   - ET POLICY — policy violations (cleartext passwords, etc.)
#
# Rule that fired during testing:
#   SID 2024364: ET SCAN Possible Nmap User-Agent Observed
#   (alert tcp any any -> any any (msg:"ET SCAN Possible Nmap User-Agent Observed";
#    flow:established,to_server; content:"Nmap Scripting Engine"; ... classtype:network-scan;)
#
# To reload rules:
#   sudo suricata-update && sudo systemctl reload suricata
#
# Evidence of rule effectiveness: evidence/after/fast_log_nmap.txt
